  "notes": [
    "User-specified HP bands at reference level 63: wolves 6300–7000; both bird groups 7000–9000.",
    "Per-variant distribution, attacks, defenses and shared growth rates are initial proposals, not combat-validated values.",
    "HP and attack are independent: high-HP variants may also have high attack.",
    "Numbers describe world monsters, not captured pets. Pet scaling and capture/reset rules are pending.",
    "Felsenflügel and Mondvariante remain working names; neither earlier name suggestion is silently finalized.",
    "No rarity, taming permissions, drops, final XP rewards or new creature abilities are assigned.",
    "Golems use a provisional level-60 anchor: 9800 HP, 350 physical attack, 250 physical and magical defense. The old golem dummy defined HP only; attack and defenses are new proposals.",
    "Ice golem starts with the same numerical profile as stone; ice behavior remains open. Giants multiply HP, physical attack and both defenses by 1.10; volcanic golem by 1.25. Attack/movement speed and rewards are not increased.",
    "Volcanic golem is a small miniboss concept; final basalt/obsidian material, distinct behavior and abilities remain open.",
    "Wolf group 2 contains offspring and pack leaders. Pack leaders exist for all seven adult wolf variants, with 1.10 HP, physical attack and both defenses at the same level. Tempo is unchanged.",
    "Young and pups only for forest wolf, gray wolf and frostclaw wolf. Young use 0.50 at their own level and spawn 2 levels below local adults; pups use 0.40 and spawn 4 levels below adults. Clamp placement to level 1. Placement is design metadata, not an implemented spawner. Never apply level difference twice.",
    "Wolf group 2 is the user-defined logical grouping for offspring and leaders; concrete Unreal models remain open. Both bird groups preserve their collected names."
  ],
